       when  pptthhrreeaadd__ccrreeaattee(3)  is called with a second argument that is NULL.
       The default attributes are set using the attributes supplied in  _*_a_t_t_r,
       a  previously initialized thread attributes object.  Note the following
       details about the supplied attributes object:

       •  The attribute settings in the object must be valid.

       •  The _s_t_a_c_k _a_d_d_r_e_s_s attribute must not be set in the object.

       •  Setting the _s_t_a_c_k _s_i_z_e attribute to zero  means  leave  the  default
          stack size unchanged.

       The  pptthhrreeaadd__ggeettaattttrr__ddeeffaauulltt__nnpp()  function  initializes the thread at‐
       tributes object referred to by _a_t_t_r so that it contains the default at‐
       tributes used for thread creation.

